#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: 1,234,567
#> pause: 45
#> must: 1,234,567
#> must: 12,345
#> must: 999
#> not: 1234567
#> not: ERROR parsing
#> source: \B[0-9]\{3\}\>
# 14. Put commas in big numbers. Pement: gsed ':a;s/\B[0-9]\{3\}\>/,&/;ta'
# \B is "not at a word boundary", [0-9]\{3\} three digits, \> the end of a
# word: so the pattern is "three digits that end a number but don't start
# it". A comma goes in front of them (& is the match) and t loops until no
# such group is left. 999 has no digit before its three, so it is untouched.
# Try: feed it 1234.5678 and see why the sheet has a separate decimal version.
:a
s/\B[0-9]\{3\}\>/,&/;ta

#DATA
1234567
12345
999
